{
    // Newest-only slice of the WHOLE test matrix for `validate:tests:newest`, in a
    // SINGLE tsgo program (not the per-db split of ./tsconfig.<db>.json). It keeps
    // the version set the agent works with day-to-day — every db's `newest/` +
    // `types.negative/` (mirrors the runner's `--run-versions newest`), plus the
    // shared infra (lib, templates, db/general, each db's runners.ts) and src —
    // and drops the older version tiers (oldest/, 8_000_000/, …) and domain/.
    //
    // A single program over the newest set fits in far less RAM than the full
    // whole-matrix `validate:tests` (which now peaks past 17 GB in tsgo and OOMs):
    // the older tiers + domain are exactly the bulk that pushes it over, so newest
    // peaks ~6 GB — comfortably in RAM. One invocation, one pass/fail: it's the
    // fast inner typecheck loop. (Wall time is a touch slower than the 6-way
    // `validate:tests:per-db` split, whose small per-db programs parallelise
    // better, but the single pass is simpler and its RAM headroom is the point.)
    // The full per-db `validate:tests:per-db` stays the pre-push / CI gate.
    //
    // The newest set is expressed by INCLUDE, so a newly added version-tier folder
    // is auto-excluded here with no edit.
    "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
    "include": [
        "lib/**/*.ts",
        "templates/**/*.ts",
        "db/general/**/*.ts",
        "db/*/newest/**/*.ts",
        "db/*/types.negative/**/*.ts",
        "db/*/runners.ts",
        "../src/**/*.ts"
    ]
}
